-- S0-3 (review round of `ffi-lower-and-link`): the builtin-name exemption
-- requires a SIGNATURE match, not just a name match.
--
-- `log` is a real `stdlib/runtime.mdk` catalog name (`Float -> Float`, the
-- natural logarithm), and a catalog name is lowered as the BUILTIN whatever the
-- local row claims -- `ffiExternRows` (compiler/ir/core_ir_lower.mdk) subtracts
-- the catalog from the FFI index outright and `emitApp` tests `isAnyExtern`
-- before the FFI arm, neither of which reads any typecheck verdict.  While the
-- exemption was keyed on the bare name alone, this declaration compiled to
-- `call double @mdk_log(double <String cell pointer>)` at exit 0 and the
-- author's own C `log` was never called or even declared.
--
-- 🚨 THE CELL THIS MUST BE READ WITH IS `ffi_cross_builtin_name_accept.mdk`
-- (`getEnv` redeclared COMPATIBLY, still accepted).  The two differ only in
-- whether the local type-head shape agrees with the catalog row's, so a fix that
-- simply deleted the exemption would show green here and red there.
--
-- ⚠️ Note what this signature does NOT fail: `String` and `Unit` are both in the
-- FFI-ABI.md section 1 crossable set and the row names `FFI`, so routing this
-- declaration through the crossable and label guards instead of rejecting it
-- would change nothing at all.  That is why this is its own rule.
extern log : String -> <FFI "mylog"> Unit

main : <IO, FFI "mylog"> Unit
main =
  let _ = log "hello from my C logger"
  println "done"
